Day 12 – Docker Networking & Docker Compose

1. Docker Networking – Container Communication

What is a Docker Network?

A Docker network allows containers to communicate with each other. For example, a web application container needs to communicate with a database container.

A user-defined bridge network is useful because Docker provides automatic DNS resolution. This means containers on the same network can communicate using their container names instead of manually finding IP addresses.

Hands-on Practice

Step 1: Create a custom network

docker network create app-network

Step 2: Run two containers on the same network

docker run -d --name container1 --network app-network nginx

docker run -d --name container2 --network app-network nginx

Step 3: Enter the first container

docker exec -it container1 bash

Step 4: Test communication

curl http://container2

Result: Received the Nginx HTML response.

What I understood: Docker's internal DNS resolved the name "container2" automatically because both containers were connected to the same user-defined network.

