6. Docker Compose Lifecycle Management

Commands Practiced

sudo docker compose logs website
sudo docker compose stop website
sudo docker compose ps -a
sudo docker compose start website
sudo docker compose ps
sudo docker compose restart website
sudo docker compose ps
sudo docker compose down

What Each Command Does

- "logs": Displays output generated by the service's container. Useful for troubleshooting.
- "stop": Stops a running container but keeps it available.
- "start": Starts an existing stopped container.
- "restart": Stops and starts an existing container.
- "ps": Shows the status of containers belonging to the Compose project.
- "down": Stops and removes the project's containers and default network.

Important difference:

"stop" does not remove the container, while "down" removes the Compose project's containers and default network.

Also, "docker compose down" does not delete the original host directory used by a bind mount.

