7. Data Persistence Verification

What is Data Persistence?

Data persistence means keeping important data available even when a container is stopped or removed.

A container has its own writable filesystem layer. Data stored only in that layer can disappear when the container is removed.

A bind mount keeps the original files on the host machine.

Hands-on Verification

After running:

sudo docker compose down

Checked the host-side files:

ls ~/day12-compose/website

cat ~/day12-compose/website/index.html

Result: The original HTML file was still present.

This helped me understand why bind mounts are useful when application files need to remain outside the container lifecycle.

