8. Important Concepts for Revision

Topic| What I understood
User-defined Bridge| Connects containers and provides automatic name resolution within the shared network.
Docker Internal DNS| Resolves container names to their IP addresses on a shared user-defined network.
Docker Compose| Manages application services using a YAML configuration file.
YAML| A structured, human-readable configuration format.
Port Mapping| Forwards traffic from a host port to a container port.
Bind Mount| Connects a specific host directory to a container directory.
Read-only Mount| Allows reading mounted files but prevents writes through that mount.
Data Persistence| Keeps important data outside the container's writable layer.
Compose Lifecycle| Manages starting, stopping, restarting and removing services.


